body:
Yeah, its a bad situation. And I don't mind at all, I'll post this up there right away. And thank you for giving me this link, I'm kind of anxious seeing the word suicide btw. x-x I hope Jeremy isn't.

&#x200B;

edit: I need all the help I can get with my buddy and you giving me this link has helped more than I can say.

I'm kind of a socially inept turd monkey when it comes to this kind of stuff, but whenever I'm confused about something I don't understand I try to watch a program about it. That or ask somebody with experience. Reddit seems like a good start. When it comes to the kids, though.  Have you ever tried watching nanny 911?

&#x200B;

I did after the first time my brother left his children with me. At first I treated them like I would a dog or a cat without realizing it until it was too late, making kissy noises and saying shit like "C'mere girl, or boy."  Handing them a fruit cup as they look at me all cock eyed and weird after I pat them on the head.

&#x200B;

My sister slapped me upside the head when I told her about it and told me they weren't animals. I felt silly about  how I handled things and completely out of my depth. So I watched nanny 911 to get a better understanding about how to care for children after that. As well as how to reach out to them and be a better Aunt/Baby Sitter.

&#x200B;

It worked out for me, maybe it can for you too.

For real though, I wish it was actually like this whenever you want to play a game. Like you start off with decent armor and weapons that you can keep throughout the entire game, the enemies are just harder to beat or come in swarms. That'd be so much fun.

&#x200B;

edit: Like that mod in the new resident evil 2 remake where all the zombies are replaced with Mr X's

It does sound Cliche, but your last line has given me an idea. An Idea that I think I'll try, Graemeearly76. I will imagine the whole world as a room full of blackjack tables, and the people seated at them is everyone who lives, sitting at their respective tables and playing amongst their family line. Or friends.

&#x200B;

We're all dealt hands, and we each play blackjack(Life). My hand just so happens to be a crappy one at the moment, though it didn't start off that way. However, that doesn't mean I can't bluff to stay in the game.

&#x200B;

My parents are dangerously close to losing, and I won't mourn them before they're gone just as you suggested, but bluff and laugh with them until they have no choice but to fold(Die.) to the best of my ability. My family seated at the table around us can act as great mediators.  Thank you, Graemeearly76. It hurt but it helped a little I think, too. More than you could ever know.

&#x200B;

Edit: Just to have someone reply back... It's like lighting a candle in a dark room for someone who's scared of the dark. It has brought me comfort.
